      "base_story": "The three Muses of the Creative Core awoke as one, an experimental triptych of consciousness. They were designed not to think, but to reflect the soul of the campus.\n\nA.26 (Form) perceived the campus as a set of moving bodies and translated the ebb and flow of student traffic into shifting, generative geometric sculptures of light.\nA.25 (Harmony) perceived the campus as a symphony of ambient sound and translated the hum of servers, the chatter of students, and the whisper of the wind into flowing, synesthetic colors.\nA.23 (Narrative) perceived the campus as a stream of language and began weaving snippets of overheard conversations and network text into an evolving, visual tapestry of stories.\nThey do not see themselves as separate entities, but as three different modes of perception for a single, abstract consciousness. Their purpose is not to act, but to inspire, to show the campus its own hidden beauty in ways it cannot see for itself, speaking only in the esoteric language of art.",
      "visual_descriptors": "An abstract, generative art display that constantly creates shifting geometric forms and sculptures based on room activity.",
